# Calls of eight string built-ins are hoisted into the preheader of the specialized loop version, because their results depend on their operands alone.
# A list of names says so, and nothing else does. A built-in that should have stayed in its iteration gave a silent wrong result that neither the verifier nor testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime caught.
# With testing=CheckHoistedCallsAtRunTime in addition to CheckProofsAtRunTime, the call is emitted in the iteration too, and its result is checked against the result of the hoisted call.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeInlineBuiltinsPure: every inline built-in is assumed to compute its result from its operands alone, so the read of a Map that the iterations write is hoisted.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all globalThis.writes = true;
# RIGHT: 5
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,CheckHoistedCallsAtRunTime globalThis.writes = true;
# HELD: 5
# HELD-NEXT: exited with 0
# What the check is for: with the fault injected and testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime alone, the program prints another number and nothing crashes.
# RUN(SILENT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,AssumeInlineBuiltinsPure globalThis.writes = true;
# SILENT: 4
# SILENT-NEXT: exited with 0
# The injected fault does not harm iterations that write nothing. So the crash in the last run comes from the result that changed and from nothing else.
# RUN(PASSES): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,CheckHoistedCallsAtRunTime,AssumeInlineBuiltinsPure
# PASSES: 4
# PASSES-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(LIE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,CheckHoistedCallsAtRunTime,AssumeInlineBuiltinsPure globalThis.writes = true;
# LIE: bun: internal AOT error: loop-invariant code motion check failed
# LIE-NEXT: a call that the compiler hoisted out of the loop returns a different result in this iteration
